POSSIBLE HYBRID OPPORTUNITY

At First Federal Bank, our core values speak to the heart of our organization and are the essence of our company’s identity. Everything we do is centered around our community
, customer service
, our stability
, and being trustworthy
. These values support our mission and vision, shape our culture, and provide a foundation for the future.

Offering a dynamic benefit package that includes but is not limited to:

Four Medical Plan Offerings to choose from
Employer HSA Contributions (Coverage/Plan exclusions)
Employer Provided Life Insurance Policy
Annual Health Incentive
Annual Wellness Reimbursement
Tuition Reimbursement program
Generous Match 401k Retirement Plan
Paid Sick Leave
Paid Vacation Leave
11 Paid Holidays Based on the Federal Reserve Calendar

If you are ready to take on a challenging and rewarding role; we invite you to apply for this exciting opportunity.

Job Purpose

Designs, develops, automates and maintains internally built applications, integrations and unattended automation that advance the Bank’s operations. Operates as an individual contributor on the Development and Automation team, delivering innovative and creative solutions through a secure, governed development life cycle while protecting the long-term stability of the Bank’s systems, data and customer trust.

Essential Functions

Provide Reliability by developing, testing and maintaining applications and automation that protect the performance, integrity and availability of the Bank’s systems and data;
Assure proper Responsiveness to business needs by delivering solutions through an Agile/Scrum process of sprints, feature branches and pull requests, prioritizing and adjusting work to meet business objectives;
Develop, script and maintain interactive applications, API endpoints and scheduled tasks on the Bank’s development platforms, primarily using PowerShell;
Design and support unattended automation, scripts and integrations that reduce manual effort and improve operational efficiency;
Follow the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) and Automation procedures, including risk classification, data classification, secure coding, code review, testing and change management;
Participate in development projects to deliver Tangibles, including but not limited to building, configuring and deploying applications, endpoints, containers and related automation;
Protect the confidentiality, integrity and availability of Bank and customer information; ensure no non-public information is stored in application, file or database environments and that data is accessed securely from the system of record;
Implement authentication and role-based access through Active Directory, manage secrets securely, and apply secure coding practices aligned to the Bank’s standards;
Log all project work, change management tasks and support interactions in the ticketing system and provide Assurance that changes and resolutions are completed timely and in accordance with established procedures;
Support production issues, including approved emergency corrections (hotfixes) to production, ensuring such changes are documented in the ticketing system and reconciled to source control;
Create, update and maintain documentation of applications, automation and the application inventory/risk register;
Collaborate with the Technology Officer, business owners and other IT staff, providing Empathy by listening to and understanding business needs and translating them into practical, well-supported solutions;
Adhere to IT department strategies, processes, policies and procedures;
Demonstrate accuracy, thoroughness, quality and orderliness in performing work assignments;
Provide the best service to our customers with innovative and creative solutions.

Essential Duties

The essential functions listed above are representative of the core responsibilities of this position and are not intended to be an exhaustive list. As business needs, technologies and priorities evolve, this role is expected to perform additional related duties, tasks and responsibilities reasonably necessary to accomplish the objectives of the position and to support the Development and Automation team and the Bank’s overall goals, whether or not such duties are specifically described herein. All such duties are considered essential to the role.

Job Requirements

Minimum 3–5 years of related software development or automation experience with a Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems or a related field; or 5–10 years of related software development or automation experience in lieu of a degree;
Extensive, hands-on experience developing and scripting in PowerShell;
Working knowledge of Git-based source control, including branching and pull-request workflows;
Familiarity with REST APIs, relational and document databases, and containerization ;
Familiarity with Active Directory authentication, SSO, OAUTH, JWT, role-based access, and secure coding and testing practices;
Must have an aptitude for troubleshooting, analyzing, and diagnosing problems;
Strong oral and written communication skills and decision-making ability;
Ability to handle changing priorities and make valuable contributions to team objectives;
Ability to work non-business hours and on-call hours as needed, including for emergency production support;
Must interact professionally with other employees, customers and suppliers;
Extended hours sitting and performing computer tasks may be required;
Must be able to complete complex projects with minimum to no supervision.
First Federal Bank is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants and employees receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.
Employees confirm they are able to perform the essential functions of this position to continue employment with First Federal Bank.
This job description may not be all-inclusive; accurate and complete. Job Descriptions are determined by the needs of the individual financial institution. Employees are expected to perform other duties as assigned and directed by management. Job Descriptions may be modified when deemed appropriate by management.

Bilingual candidates encouraged to apply.

